      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: `bessel_first` cost grows with the clamped order, so one huge bignum order hangs the VM for seconds.\n\n`(flfirst-bessel (expt 2 100) 1.0)` clamps to `i32::MAX` in `order()` and then `libm::jn` walks it (~13.87s wall in the probe; 500k-\u003e6.3ms, 1M-\u003e8.1ms, 2M-\u003e13.1ms). The comment says such orders \"are zero or infinite for every argument alike\", so the result is known without the walk.\n\nFix: short-circuit beyond a bound where the result is settled (e.g. return `0.0`/`-0.0` directly) instead of calling `jn`/`yn` with `i32::MIN`/`MAX`.",
